---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Prufrock" description="Your life. Your voice. Your book.">
  <div class="container prufrock">

    <header class="prufrock-header">
      <p class="kicker">FlowLabs</p>
      <h1>Prufrock</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="epigraph">
      <p>Do I dare<br/>Disturb the universe?<br/>In a minute there is time<br/>For decisions and revisions which a minute will reverse.</p>
      <p class="attribution">— T.S. Eliot</p>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <p>
      There is a box in your attic, or your garage, or a storage unit
      you pay for every month and never visit. Inside it are letters
      in handwriting you recognize but haven't seen in years. Photographs
      of people whose names you're starting to forget. A journal you kept
      during the worst year of your life. Your mother's recipe cards.
      Your father's margin notes in a book you didn't know he read.
    </p>

    <p>
      You have thought, more than once, about throwing it away.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Who would care?</em>
    </p>

    <p>
      And in that question lives the same hesitation Prufrock felt —
      the measuring out of a life in coffee spoons, the quiet certainty
      that the story isn't worth telling, that the universe doesn't need
      disturbing, that the peach should remain uneaten.
    </p>

    <p>
      But you would be wrong.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>
      Ship me the boxes.
    </p>

    <p>
      I photograph every page, every letter, every margin note. I scan
      the negatives and the prints. I digitize the home videos. Everything
      is transcribed — the handwriting your father scratched into the margins
      of a recovery book at 3 AM, the recipe your mother wrote on the back
      of an envelope, the journal entry you wrote the day you got sober.
    </p>

    <p>
      The AI reads what they wrote. It finds the dates they mentioned,
      the people they named, the places they went. It tags everything —
      who, when, where, and the moments that carry emotional weight
      a machine can detect but only you can confirm.
    </p>

    <p>
      It clusters the faces in your photographs. It builds a timeline
      that spans decades. It finds threads between documents that were
      in separate boxes in separate rooms, connections you couldn't see
      because the pieces were never in the same place before.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then we talk.
    </p>

    <p>
      I show you what the pipeline found. I show you the faces and
      you tell me their names. And in the telling — in the moment
      you say "that's Uncle Jerry, he was the one who..." — you
      start remembering things you forgot you knew. I'm listening.
      I'm recording. Your voice, the way you actually sound when
      you talk about the people you loved, becomes the raw material
      for everything that follows.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>What you receive</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>The Archive.</strong> Everything digitized, transcribed,
      tagged, and searchable. A timeline of your family. Your physical
      materials returned safely. The digital archive is yours forever.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>The Story.</strong> The archive, plus the threads —
      narrative arcs the AI found across your documents that you
      couldn't see when they lived in separate boxes. A session
      where I walk you through what emerged and we map
      the memoir together.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>The Companion.</strong> The story, plus an AI writing
      partner that already knows your family, your timeline, your
      threads, and your voice. You sit down and talk to it the way
      you talked to me on the call. It writes in your voice, from
      your materials. You never face a blank page. You just remember
      out loud.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>
      Prufrock also scores AI-assisted writing for voice fidelity —
      the original question that started this. <em>Does this sound
      like you?</em> If you're a consultant, a lawyer, or anyone
      who sends AI-generated writing under your own name,
      <a href="/essays/2026-03-20-your-ai-sounds-like-nowhere">read the origin story</a>.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>
      I built this because I found my dead father's recovery book
      in a box I almost threw away. He had written in the margins
      for eight years — tracking my life, noting the weather, logging
      his cancer treatments, writing my name into his prayers.
      On his amends list, my name was first.
    </p>

    <p>
      I didn't know any of that until I photographed the pages
      and let the machine read what he wrote.
    </p>

    <p>
      The boxes in your attic are not junk.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <div class="prufrock-cta">
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:robert@northwoodssentinel.com?subject=Prufrock">Get in touch</a>
        &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="https://substack.com/@chewvala">Follow on Substack</a>
      </p>
      <p class="closing">
        <em>Let us go then, you and I.</em>
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <style>
    .prufrock {
      max-width: 600px;
    }

    .prufrock-header {
      margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0 var(--spacing-lg);
    }

    .kicker {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    }

    .prufrock-header h1 {
      font-size: 3rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin: 0;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    }

    .epigraph {
      margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-xl);
      padding-left: var(--spacing-lg);
      border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
    }

    .epigraph p {
      line-height: 1.8;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .epigraph .attribution {
      margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
    }

    .prufrock h2 {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    }

    .prufrock hr {
      margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .prufrock p {
      line-height: 1.8;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .prufrock-cta {
      margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .prufrock-cta a {
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .closing {
      margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .prufrock-header h1 {
        font-size: 2.2rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
